    "updated_at": "2026-08-28T09:45:50Z",
    "body": "> Curious, so the current state of the PR defines `<link import=\"\">` rather than using `type=\"module\"`. Not objecting or anything, but why?\r\n\r\nThis came up at WHATNOT, as wanting to keep `type` for mime-types in links, and also some issues with having a module specifier instead of a URL in `href`.\r\n\r\nBy using `<link import=\"\" href=\"url.css\">` or `<link import=\"specifier\" href=\"url.css\">`, the link would act as a regular stylesheet in unsupported browsers, and as a module when supported.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/5451014413/reactions",
